      "20/09/2026 18:15 — Claude Sprint Decision\n\nPartner, select **Option 1: “S0 + S2 + transport seam (Recommended)”**.\n\nThis gives Claude the maximum useful code work without waiting for:\n\n- Customer interviews and the S1 demand gate\n- A real Xero organisation\n- Email-vendor selection\n- Positioning and pricing decisions\n\nIt fixes the most serious production defects: shutdown, evidence portability, misleading statuses, durable tenant/token persistence, restart hydration, webhook worker, uninstall processing and the notification interface.\n\nIf Claude asks for extra instructions, answer:\n\n> Proceed with Option 1: S0 + S2 + vendor-neutral transport seam. Do not select a specific email vendor and do not implement a fake sender. Preserve all existing history, finding IDs and traceability. Produce updated code, tests, mutation gates, product workbook, sprint tracker, release notes, coverage evidence, evidence manifest and packaged ZIP. Keep S1 and all live/customer validation work explicitly blocked, not Done."
     ]
